<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gurganj</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gurganj, also known as Urgench, was a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a>. It was a prosperous centre of trade and learning on routes linking Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> with the wider world. The city was besieged and destroyed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> during their conquest of the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gurganj.jpg" alt="Gurganj" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Atilin at French Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Urgench.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
